<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept cocoa bean imports rise 8.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept cocoa bean imports rise 8.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's cocoa bean imports in September totalled 5,382 tonnes, up by 8.7 percent from a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday. The breakdown is as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Sept 96	 Aug 96	 Sept 95</p>
<p> Total		5,382	   4,794	  4,952</p>
<p> Major suppliers (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Ghana		3,660	   3,117	  3,935</p>
<p> Venezuela	    397	     546	    182</p>
<p> Ecuador		286	     274	    227</p>
<p>Cumulative cocoa bean imports in the first nine months of calendar 1996 were 42,929 tonnes, against 34,921 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of other cocoa products were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Sept 96	 Aug 96	Sept 95</p>
<p> Cocoa paste	  67		167	     231</p>
<p> Defatted paste    nil		 72		73</p>
<p> Cocoa butter    1,003	    1,434	     754</p>
<p> Cocoa powder	806		690	     718</p>
<p> Chocolate</p>
<p> confectionery   2,022		909	   1,728</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
